1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:26,000
In stage one, Achilles runs those 100 metres, which takes him 10 seconds.

2
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:56,000
But in those 10 seconds, the tortoise has crawled 10 metres further.

3
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:26,000
In stage two, Achilles covers those 10 metres in 1 second, and the tortoise crawls another metre.

4
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Stage three leaves a gap of 10 centimetres, and stage four leaves just 1 centimetre.

5
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Each gap is a tenth of the one before. It shrinks forever, but it never reaches zero.

6
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:56,000
So there is always one more stage. Achilles, Zeno concludes, never catches up.

7
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:26,000
So how far does Achilles run before he draws level? Let's add up the stages.

8
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:56,000
It's 100 metres, plus 10, plus 1, plus a tenth, plus a hundredth, and so on.

9
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:26,000
The running totals are 100, then 110, then 111, then 111.1, then 111.11.

10
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:56,000
They close in on 111 and one ninth metres, with the ones repeating forever.

11
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:26,000
The times add up the same way, to 11 and one ninth seconds.

12
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:56,000
That's infinitely many stages, but they add up to a finite distance, and a finite time.

13
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:26,000
Plot distance against time, and each runner is a straight line. The lines cross at 11.1 seconds and 111.1 metres.

14
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:56,000
Zeno's stages are a staircase closing in on that crossing, and every one of them comes before it.

15
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:26,000
The moment Achilles catches up isn't one of the stages. It comes just after all of them.

16
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:56,000
It's often said that Zeno thought infinitely many pieces must add up to something infinite.

17
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:26,000
But no ancient source has Zeno discussing an infinite sum at all.

18
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:56,000
In Simplishius's report, his worry is that it is impossible to traverse an infinite number of things in a finite time.

19
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:26,000
So the puzzle isn't the total. It's how anyone can finish infinitely many steps, with no last one.

20
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Zeno's dichotomy makes the same point without a tortoise.
